  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"
      }
     ],
     "value": "An adhesion molecule that interacts with extracellular matrix molecules in developing teeth and may play important roles in differentiation and maintenance of odontoblasts as well as in dentin formation"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "FUNCTION"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Interacts with heparin, FBLN1, FN1 and DSPP. Preferentially binds dental mesenchyme cells and odontoblasts but not dental epithelial cells or nondental cells. Binding requires a heparan sulfate-containing receptor on the cell surface as well as an integrin (By similarity)"
    }
   ],
